{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a7f3c1e0-5b2d-4d9a-9c31-0f2a6b8e4d10",
    "name": "OpsPortal — Mini ERP + CRM",
    "description": "Full API for the OpsPortal case-study project (Django + DRF).\n\n## How to use\n1. Pick the **Local (Docker)** environment or leave `base_url` at its default `http://localhost:8080`.\n2. Run **Auth → Login (admin)**. Its test script stores `access_token`, `refresh_token` and `user_id` as collection variables, and every other request inherits the bearer token.\n3. Run **Seeded lookups → Fetch first customer / product** once — it fills `customer_id` and `product_id` so the challan requests work out of the box.\n\nAll list endpoints are paginated (`count`, `page`, `page_size`, `total_pages`, `next`, `previous`, `results`) and every error uses the envelope `{ success:false, error:{ code, message, details } }`.\n\n### Test logins\n| Role | Username | Password |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Admin | admin | Admin@12345 |\n| Sales | sales | Sales@12345 |\n| Warehouse | warehouse | Warehouse@12345 |\n| Accounts | accounts | Accounts@12345 |",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{access_token}}", "type": "string" }]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Nothing global to do; Login stores the token for the rest of the run."
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:8080", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "access_token", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "refresh_token", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "user_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "customer_id", "value": "1", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "product_id", "value": "1", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "challan_id", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (admin)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('returns a token pair and the user', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('access');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('refresh');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.user).to.have.property('role');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('access_token', body.access);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('refresh_token', body.refresh);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('user_id', body.user.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"admin\",\n  \"password\": \"Admin@12345\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/login/", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "login", ""] },
            "description": "Accepts a username **or** an e-mail address. Returns `{access, refresh, user}`."
          }
        },
